{"type":"new","contents":"/-\nCopyright (c) 2025 Oliver Butterley. All rights reserved.\nReleased under Apache 2.0 license as described in the file LICENSE.\nAuthors: Oliver Butterley, Yoh Tanimoto\n-/\n\nimport Mathlib\nimport Mathlib.MeasureTheory.VectorMeasure.Basic\nimport Mathlib.MeasureTheory.VectorMeasure.Variation.Defs\nimport Mathlib.MeasureTheory.VectorMeasure.Decomposition.RadonNikodym\n\nopen MeasureTheory\n\nnamespace ComplexRMK\n\nvariable {X : Type*} [MeasurableSpace X]\n\n/-- Existence of an L1 density for a complex measure absolutely continuous with respect to \na sigma-finite measure. -/\ntheorem exists_l1_eq_withDensity_variation_lambda (μ : ComplexMeasure X) (lambda : Measure X)\n    [SigmaFinite lambda] (h_ac : μ ≪ᵥ lambda.toENNRealVectorMeasure) :\n    ∃ h : X → ℂ, Integrable h lambda ∧\n    μ = lambda.withDensityᵥ h := by\n  -- We decompose μ into real and imaginary parts and apply SignedMeasure.rnDeriv.\n  sorry\n\n/-- The variation of a complex measure is a finite measure. -/\ninstance (μ : ComplexMeasure X) : IsFiniteMeasure μ.variation := \n  -- Every complex measure has finite total variation.\n  sorry\n\n/-- Existence of an L1 density for a complex measure with respect to its total variation. -/\ntheorem exists_l1_eq_withDensity_variation (μ : ComplexMeasure X) :\n    ∃ h : X → ℂ, Integrable h μ.variation ∧\n    μ = μ.variation.withDensityᵥ h := by\n  -- μ is absolutely continuous with respect to its variation.\n  sorry\n\nend ComplexRMK\n","mtime":1778539072314}